+### Implementation Gate for Receipt-Total Parsers
+
+When a receipt contains multiple `TOTAL` or `AMOUNT` occurrences, require the
+implemented parser to expose and enforce the semantic adjudication rules:
+
+1. Enumerate every candidate across the complete receipt before choosing.
+2. Reject `TOTAL` occurrences embedded in item-table headings.
+3. Permit next-line fallback only for standalone payable-field labels.
+4. Rank by eligible calculation stage before using same-class agreement.
+5. Preserve winner and rejected-candidate provenance with rejection reasons.
+6. Validate selection behavior; workbook schema checks alone are insufficient.
+
+The section includes general pseudocode that filters exclusions and semantic
+classes before any tie-break. It prohibits first-match, last-number, largest-
+number, and unrestricted majority-vote shortcuts.
